From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] EXPERIMENT: arm64: dts: rockchip: pinetab2: fastest vdd_cpu slew

Diagnostic. The tablet resets on any VSEL write to the TCS4525 under heavy
load, however small the step, while reads and all other bus traffic are
fine. The slew is programmed to the slowest setting (2.3 mV/us); program
the fastest (18.7 mV/us) so the chip spends the least possible time in a
DVS transition per write.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [diagnostic experiment]

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
@@ -397,7 +397,7 @@
 		regulator-min-microvolt = <800000>;
 		regulator-max-microvolt = <1150000>;
 		regulator-initial-mode = <FAN53555_MODE_FORCED_PWM>;
-		regulator-ramp-delay = <2300>;
+		regulator-ramp-delay = <18700>;
 		/*
 		 * The ramp delay alone gives the OPP core no margin between
 		 * the voltage arriving and the clock going up, and the SoC
